; Three support libraries, deliberately split by dependency (gh-ocannl-600). [test_utils] stays
; below [ocannl] -- [arrayjit.utils], [arrayjit.ir] and [arrayjit.verdict], no backends and no
; tensor layer -- because tests like config_scan_lexing and test_ndarray link nothing more;
; [ll_test] links [ocannl], for the hand-built-Low_level harness.
;
; [arrayjit.utils] and [arrayjit.verdict] arrived with the generated-artifact reader (gh-ocannl-655),
; which resolves [build_files/] paths and reports a missing or overwritten artifact as a verdict.
; Neither widens the set of tests that can link [test_utils]: [arrayjit.ir] already depends on
; [arrayjit.utils], and [arrayjit.verdict] depends on nothing but base and stdio.
;
; [verdict] (gh-ocannl-601) depends on nothing but base and stdio, and is the one support library
; that is PUBLIC, because the tests of both packages report verdicts through it and a
; package-filtered build cannot see across the boundary. `dune build -p <pkg>` -- what each .opam
; file's with-test command runs -- disables the stanzas of every package it did not select and
; resolves those libraries from the INSTALLED ones instead, so a PRIVATE library assigned to
; `arrayjit` is unresolvable from the neural tests under `-p neural_nets_lib` (Codex, round 2), and
; assigning it to `neural_nets_lib` breaks the arrayjit tests the same way under `-p arrayjit`.
; Unpackaged does not work either: a private library attached to a package -- `ll_test`,
; `operations_tutorials` -- may not depend on an unpackaged one. So it installs, as
; `arrayjit.verdict`, and every dependant spells it by that public name: under the filter the
; private name is not what is on disk.

(library
 (name verdict)
 (public_name arrayjit.verdict)
 (modules verdict)
 (libraries base stdio))

(library
 (name test_utils)
 (package neural_nets_lib)
 (modules test_utils config_key_scan cache_dir_scan dune_stanza_scan generated)
 (libraries
  base
  stdio
  arrayjit.utils
  arrayjit.ir
  arrayjit.verdict
  compiler-libs.common
  sexplib))

(library
 (name ll_test)
 (package neural_nets_lib)
 (modules ll_test)
 (libraries base stdio ocannl arrayjit.verdict))
